# Portal security

The portal is a client of one API. It is not a second backend. Load `web-security` before rendering user text, touching the session, or adding a redirect.

| Risk | Required control |
| --- | --- |
| XSS | Render names, notes, and errors as React text. No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, `innerHTML`, `eval`, or `javascript:` URLs |
| CSRF | `credentials: "include"` on API calls. The `/api/v1` rewrite in `next.config.ts` is the only forwarder; no `src/app/api` route handler |
| Token theft | Access token stays in memory. No `localStorage` or `sessionStorage`. No `NEXT_PUBLIC_` secret, Mongo URL, or JWT secret |
| SSRF | Call only `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`. No Route Handler and no fetch of a URL from the query string |
| Open redirect | Redirects go to `/login` or `/dashboard` only |
| Clickjacking | Do not frame untrusted HTML. `target="_blank"` uses `rel="noopener noreferrer"` |

User content is text. A chart tooltip gets the same string the table cell gets. Do not parse notes as HTML.
